  _globals['_TOOLSERVICE'].methods_by_name['ListAvailableTools']._loaded_options = None
  _globals['_TOOLSERVICE'].methods_by_name['ListAvailableTools']._serialized_options = b'\222A\330\002\n\005Tools\0221List all tools for a connected account identifier\032QLists all tools for a given Connected Account Identifier. Identifier is required.J*\n\003200\022#\n!Paginated list of available toolsJ:\n\003400\0223\n1Invalid request - missing or malformed identifierJB\n\003401\022;\n9Authentication required - missing or invalid access tokenJ\035\n\003404\022\026\n\024Identifier not found\202\265\030\002\030\004\372\322\344\223\002\t\022\007PREVIEW\202\323\344\223\002\031\022\027/api/v1/tools/available'
  _globals['_TOOLSERVICE'].methods_by_name['SearchTools']._loaded_options = None
  _globals['_TOOLSERVICE'].methods_by_name['SearchTools']._serialized_options = b'\222A\213\r\n\005Tools\022\025Search tools by query\032\303\nRanks tools in the environment against a natural-language query and returns the best matches. Use this to let an agent (or a dashboard) discover which tool fits a job to be done before executing it. Results are drawn from the tools of every connection enabled in the environment and ranked by relevance. When an `identifier` is supplied, each result also carries a `connections` list covering the connections for that tool\'s provider that this identifier has an account on \342\200\224 each entry has its own readiness state and connected_account_id \342\200\224 `ready` (usable now, safe to pass connected_account_id to ExecuteTool), `needs_reauth` (an account exists but its token expired), or `needs_connection` (an account exists but is disconnected or otherwise inactive). The connected_account_id is always returned for a listed entry regardless of readiness state, so the caller can reference or manage the account even when it isn\'t usable yet; only `ready` means it is safe to execute with. A connection this identifier has never connected at all is left out of the list entirely rather than listed as needs_connection \342\200\224 an empty `connections` array (`[]`) means this identifier does not have any connection at all for this tool\'s provider, not an error. Returns the ranked tool name, provider, description, relevance score, and per-connection readiness.J\223\001\n\003200\022\213\001\n]Ranked tools matching the query, with per-identifier readiness when an identifier is supplied\022*\n(\032&.scalekit.v1.tools.SearchToolsResponseJK\n\003400\022D\nBInvalid request - the query is empty or exceeds the maximum lengthJB\n\003401\022;\n9Authentication required - missing or invalid access token\202\265\030\002\030d\372\322\344\223\002\t\022\007PREVIEW\202\323\344\223\002\031\"\024/api/v1/tools:search:\001*'
  _globals['_TOOLSERVICE'].methods_by_name['SetToolDefault']._loaded_options = None
