  _globals['_TOOLSERVICE'].methods_by_name['ExecuteTool']._loaded_options = None
  _globals['_TOOLSERVICE'].methods_by_name['ExecuteTool']._serialized_options = b'\222A\264\010\n\014Tool Calling\022(Execute a tool using a connected account\032\317\003Executes a tool action using authentication credentials from a connected account. Specify the tool by name and provide required parameters as JSON. The connected account can be identified by ID, or by combination of organization/user, connector, and identifier. Returns the execution result data and a unique execution ID for tracking. Use this endpoint to perform actions like sending emails, creating calendar events, or managing resources in external services.Jq\n\003200\022j\n<Tool executed successfully with result data and execution ID\022*\n(\032&.scalekit.v1.tools.ExecuteToolResponseJz\n\003400\022s\nqInvalid request - occurs when tool name is missing, parameters are malformed, or tool definition validation failsJB\n\003401\022;\n9Authentication required - missing or invalid access tokenJv\n\003404\022o\nmTool or connected account not found - occurs when the specified tool name or connected account does not existJ}\n\003500\022v\ntTool execution failed - occurs when the external service returns an error or the tool encounters a runtime exception\202\265\030\034\n\030agent_connectors:execute\030d\202\323\344\223\002\031\"\024/api/v1/execute_tool:\001*'
  _globals['_TOOLSERVICE'].methods_by_name['RefreshTools']._loaded_options = None
  _globals['_TOOLSERVICE'].methods_by_name['RefreshTools']._serialized_options = b'\222A\276\t\n\005Tools\022%Refresh tools for a connected account\032\224\005Resyncs the cached tool catalog for a custom Model Context Protocol (MCP) connected account by re-querying the upstream connector\'s tool list. Use this endpoint when the upstream connector has added, renamed, or removed tools and the cached catalog has gone stale between the incidental resyncs that happen on account creation, reauthentication, and metadata updates. Identify the connected account either by its ID, or by the combination of connector and identifier (optionally scoped by organization or user). New and changed tools are upserted and tools no longer present upstream are removed. Returns the full refreshed tool list for the connected account.J\227\001\n\003200\022\217\001\n`Tools refreshed successfully; includes the full tool list for the connected account after resync\022+\n)\032\'.scalekit.v1.tools.RefreshToolsResponseJ\247\001\n\003400\022\237\001\n\234\001Invalid request - occurs when no connected account can be resolved from the supplied fields, or the resolved connected account is not a custom MCP connectorJB\n\003401\022;\n9Authentication required - missing or invalid access tokenJo\n\003404\022h\nfConnected account not found - no connected account matches the supplied ID or connector and identifier\202\265\030\034\n\030agent_connectors:execute\030d\372\322\344\223\002\t\022\007PREVIEW\202\323\344\223\002\032\"\025/api/v1/tools:refresh:\001*'
